Venetium 0072 - no "you'll need Windows 10" banner on Windows 8 / 8.1.
Chromium 150 calls every Windows below 10 obsolete (ObsoleteSystem::IsObsoleteNowOrSoon, Windows kernel32 version) and
then shows "To get future Venetium updates, you'll need Windows 10 or later. This computer is using Windows 8.1." under
the toolbar at every start, a note on the settings About page, and an upgrade-detector hint. Venetium runs on Windows
RT 8.0 / 8.1 (the thumb2 build) and keeps updating it, so the check is always false. Windows 10 never saw the banner.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/obsolete_system/obsolete_system_win.cc b/chrome/browser/obsolete_system/obsolete_system_win.cc
index 689026a..536d21d 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/obsolete_system/obsolete_system_win.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/obsolete_system/obsolete_system_win.cc
@@ -22,16 +22,15 @@ base::win::Version GetRealOSVersion() {
   return base::win::OSInfo::Kernel32Version();
 }
 
-bool IsObsoleteOsVersion() {
-  return GetRealOSVersion() < base::win::Version::WIN10;
-}
-
 }  // namespace
 
 namespace ObsoleteSystem {
 
 bool IsObsoleteNowOrSoon() {
-  return IsObsoleteOsVersion();
+  // Venetium 0072: Windows 8 / 8.1 are supported (the thumb2 build for Windows
+  // RT 8.x gets Venetium's updates), so no "you'll need Windows 10" banner,
+  // settings note or upgrade-detector hint.
+  return false;
 }
 
